<title>USA: Brent crude steady in thin U.S. aftermarket.</title>
<headline>Brent crude steady in thin U.S. aftermarket.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Sea Brent crude oil was steady in thin late U.S. trading on Friday, dealers said.</p>
<p>One October exchange-for-physical deal was done at $18.95 a barrel for 50 lots, putting the cash level at around $19.00 factoring in the recent five-cent premium of cash over paper.</p>
<p>October Brent closed at $19.01 on London's IPE.</p>
<p>September/October Brent traded at minus nine cents a barrel.</p>
<p>--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
